  m_text: 'Habitat: Sharks inhabit oceans worldwide, from shallow coastal waters
    to the deep sea.


    Diet: Depending on the species, sharks eat fish, squid,
    crustaceans, or marine mammals.


    Movement: Sharks use powerful tails for
    propulsion and fins for balance and steering.


    Unique Characteristics: Sharks
    have skeletons made of cartilage instead of bone. Many species can detect weak
    electrical signals produced by other animals.


    Fun Fact: Sharks have existed
    for more than 400 million years!'
